fix GC: seed the pinned pre-arming region in the MINOR mark (#34, definitive).

Root cause (proven by instrumentation in fix-gc-repro): every "missed edge" parent
is a PINNED pre-arming object (id < track_from) -- the compiled screen lambda + its
captured __drawDep library, binding cells, interned scaffolding -- that acquires NEW
young referents as evaluation continues (re-published binding cells, lazily-installed
merge_attrs.flattened edges, re-forced attr_access results). The write barrier does
NOT reliably capture these: it is a no-op before GC arming (collect_enabled=false),
and its single remembered-set entry is consumed + cleared every minor (remsetClear).
The minor mark seeds only markRoots + the remembered set; it NEVER walks the pinned
region [0, track_from). So a live young child reachable ONLY from a pinned parent is
unmarked and swept -> "minor mark not closed -- missed edge" panic (release: UAF).

Majors are already correct: collectMajor calls seedPinnedRegion (markObject over the
whole pinned region). The minor must do the equivalent YOUNG-GATED: markRemsetSource
walks each pinned object's edges and marks only its YOUNG children (the minor gate in
Tracer stops at old boundaries), so the cost is O(pinned outgoing edges), NOT
O(old heap). track_from is ~8192 on the badge -> trivial.

This SUPERSEDES gc-remset-young-source.patch (Fix A): the barrier never fires for
these pinned->young edges at all, so recording young sources could not help -- and
recording every young source bloated the remset into multi-second minor collects on
draw-heavy frames. Drop Fix A; this is the correct, cheap fix. (Upstream should pair
it with an incremental dirty-pinned watermark for whole-nixpkgs evals where track_from
is millions; the flat scan is the obviously-correct fix the badge needs.)

