+/// Minor analogue of `seedPinnedRegion`: the pinned pre-arming region [0, track_from)
+/// holds immortal objects that acquire NEW young referents as evaluation continues; the
+/// write barrier does not reliably capture these (no-op pre-arm; single remset entry
+/// cleared every minor), so a young-gated minor seeding only roots + remset never traces
+/// them and sweeps a live young child from a pinned parent (the "missed edge" panic).
+/// markRemsetSource marks only the source's YOUNG children and stops at old boundaries, so
+/// cost is O(pinned edges), not O(old heap). track_from is ~8192 on the badge.
+fn seedPinnedRegionMinor(heap: *ObjectHeap, tr: *gc.Tracer) void {
+    var id: types.ObjectId = 0;
+    const pinned_end = heap.collection.track_from;
+    while (id < pinned_end) : (id += 1) tr.markRemsetSource(heap, id);
+}
